\begin{align*}
r &= \frac{6}{10\tan(\theta) + \cos^2(\theta)} + \frac{6}{10\tan(\pi - \theta) + \cos^2(\pi-\theta)} \\
&= \frac{6 - 12 \cos^2(\theta)}{5\tan(\theta) + 6 - 8 \cos^2(\theta)}
\end{align*}Inasmuch as $r$ is independent of $\theta,$ the numerator must be a multiple of the denominator.  In particular, we must have $12\cos^2(\theta) = 6,$ so $\cos(\theta) = \pm\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}.$

